WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.660
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.730
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.860
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.870
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
Keep your eyes on me, okay!?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.240
I'm Kurata Sana, 12 years old in Jinbo Middle School.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.830
My manager and driver, Rei-kun. But when he was in New York he didn't like cars.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.580
The amazing white bat, Babbit.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:55.760
The child star who began his career as I started mine, Kamura Naozumi-kun.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:02.140
Whoa, he looks identical to my old friend. It's Brad! He's American.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.140
I'm Kurata Sana!

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.890
I'm Kamura Naozumi!

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.020
Enjoy yourselves.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.690
Um... about Mr. Hamilton...

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.030
Hayama?

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.820
Who is he? Your boyfriend?

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.120
Sana-chan!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.120
Are you alright? What happened?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.960
I saw it.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:29.830
What did you see?

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.540
A ghost.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.760
Experiencing
the Mysteries of Life

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.840
Ghost?!

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.050
Yup. It appeared.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.430
Hahaha! That's impossible!

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.220
Here.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.020
Thanks.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.640
Here.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.430
Thanks.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.350
- Really?
- Really.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.360
What is wrong with this house?!

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.570
Strange things keep happening since yesterday, and now we have a ghost?!

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.120
But the travel guidebook doesn't say anything about it nor what to do when one appears!

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.120
Ghosts don't exist

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.620
Hahaha! Ghosts don't exist in this world!

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.830
They do not exist...

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.050
What's wrong with everybody?
You look like you've seen a ghost.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:25.140
Actually, Ramsy-san... there's a matter which is very uncomfortable.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.640
May I know what it is?

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.890
I saw it, you know...

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.310
What is it that you saw?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.940
It could be a demon, you know... like this.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.150
Demon?

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.020
Yup. A blonde girl wearing a dress.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.650
Ahh... if it's what you're saying...

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.450
You know about it, Ramsy-san?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.240
Well... that is actually...

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.740
Ramsy...

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.620
Don't participate in idle gossip that they don't need to hear about.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.950
I'm very sorry, Madam.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:51.830
Everyone...

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:52.750
Yes!

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.330
Did everyone sleep well last night?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.250
Yes...

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.300
I think maybe it's because I swapped my pillows... but it's not that important...

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.100
Shoulders may ache.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.100
Scary person

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.350
We would like to contact Mr. Hamilton immediately...

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.150
Eh? Oh... I see...

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.560
How is it?

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.530
It seems that he's currently involved in a big project in Hollywood now...

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.450
I heard that finding him is even harder than finding the president himself.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:32.330
Mr. Hamilton is New York's Broadway's king, number one producer according to Talandalu.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.540
Sounds like he's really busy.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.040
But Hamilton's the one who called us over!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:39.380
If we don't get to see the producer, we can't take the next step...

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.420
Alright! I'll find him.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.050
Where? Hollywood?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.840
We can't just leave the situation like this!
Since I have nothing to do anyway...

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.220
Great! I can still catch the noon flight!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.520
Your first class is today.
You won't have a problem, right?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.140
Sure...

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.560
Don't be late for the 10 o'clock appointment, okay?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.440
Yes...

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.480
I'll pop by the hospital to check on Maeda-san's condition.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.900
If it's not too much trouble.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:08.030
So Rei-kun goes to look for Mr. Gary Hamilton in Hollywood.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:14.830
On the other hand, Sana-chan and Naozumi-kun depart together to attend their first class!

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:14.870
The First Meeting

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.750
What a classic car...

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.050
Sorry to keep you waiting,
please let me drive you there.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.130
- Thanks...
- If it's not too much trouble.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.390
Please...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.060
Ladies first.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.220
Thank you...

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.640
Ahaha... I'm very sorry...

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.730
This is tight...

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.220
Ehhh? Really? It's only a stomachache?

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:15.730
Yeah! It seems that Maeda-san ate something called Manhattan at the airport...

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:18.940
...and another one called New York's Lover and other just as weird stuff.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.230
This is embarrassing...

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.940
So don't worry, it's not cause he was poisoned or something.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.240
That's a relief!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.740
All right then, I'm running late for my plane so... Bye!

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.830
That was quick. It's New York all right.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.620
Oh man, Maeda-san only causes anxiety to us.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.250
But it's still a relief that he's alright.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:42.040
Although strange things keep happening since we've arrived...

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.050
Maybe we've just looked too much into it...

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.250
Sana-chan...

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.630
It's like coming to Broadway and becoming the main character of a suspense drama.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.550
That's true, but it's still a relief anyway.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:57.350
Naozumi-kun, although we can't seem to relax, let's work hard together.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.640
Yeah, we'll work hard!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.230
What happened?

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.160
A flat tire.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:17.950
It's done.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.460
Thank you.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:25.500
What the...?

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.920
Anything can happen in New York!

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.540
Tires burst in Japan too.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.500
That's true.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.130
This is the studio?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.020
Let's go then, Sana-chan.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.230
Let's go then, Naozumi-kun.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:44.480
Alright then! Show them the Japanese spinning elf power!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.150
Wait a minute, Sana-chan! Oh man...

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.940
Good morning!

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.830
Sana-chan... Sana-chan!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.450
Eh? It already started?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.500
Yeah... although it hasn't reached 10 yet...

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.750
Eh? Why is that old lady here too?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.250
Sana-chan!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:11.550
Maybe you haven't realized, but I am the technical director of Mr. Hamilton's stage plays.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.050
I've only heard of it today.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.680
Nobody waits until the exact time to come in.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.770
They come two to three hours ahead to practice by themselves.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:28.820
Everyone... let me introduce two famous artistes who have come all the way from Japan!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.240
- Famous?
- Artiste?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.320
Where are they, Michelle?

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:37.240
They're right here. Sana Kurata and Naozumi Kamura.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:42.250
Aw, come on. Michelle's such a joker.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.830
I am Kurata Sana!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.830
Sana-chan!

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.340
Whoops... what am I doing?

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.260
Babbit is feeling very good right now.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.550
Um... I'm Kamura Naozumi,
pleased to meet you.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:09:01.060
Hey Michelle, are you serious about this?
These two babies are actually movie stars?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.560
They dance very well.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:09.650
Oh yes... I want to see both of your dance moves.
I wonder if you could show them to everyone?

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.030
- Huh?
- Now? Right here?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.740
Yeah, let's see! Let's see!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:18.950
Don't, Sana-chan.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.750
I have a feeling we're being made fun of.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.330
Is... that so...

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.920
Yeah... or else things wouldn't be like this right from the start...

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.050
But I can't take this lying down...

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.800
Well, since they think we can't do it,

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.930
we'll prove them wrong by showing them something whether it's tango or waltz!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.890
Right! Naozumi-kun, gimme a beat!

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.020
Sana-chan, you're jumping into something without looking again.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.730
Everyone! Better look carefully!

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.440
I am Kurata Sana, 12 years old!

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:58.160
I've lead a very colorful life since birth.
In Gekidan Komawari, I learned this dance step!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:05.450
Dance! Dance! The time has come! To dance you need to be cheerful and happy!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.120
Ah... I'm a little embarrassed...

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.250
Naozumi-kun shall spin as well!

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.840
We're spinning, we're spinning...

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:18.840
You can't see this anywhere...
except in Kodocha!

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:24.140
Let's add in other dance steps! Twist and twist some more! I can do this too!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.360
1-2! 1-2! 1-2-3!

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:35.150
A B C D E F G H I J K L M N!

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:35.940
I'm dancing too!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.160
Dance, dance, dance, dance!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:45.120
Sana-chan's million mini-twirls!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:55.130
Twirl twirl twirl twirl...

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.510
Sana-chan!

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.930
Sana-chan! Hang in there!

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.100
It hurts...

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.560
Oil...?

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.230
Sana-chan! Are you okay?

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.530
What's "orokok anno"?

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:23.740
{parte b}

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:26.450
It's "Onna Kokoro"! (Woman's heart!)

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:30.750
We're doing the "Draw Sana Song,"
Prepare crayon and paper!

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.540
First you draw one mountain...

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.540
...then comes the water...

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.630
...there goes 2 cups...

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.630
...plus 2 earlobes...

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.630
...butterfly, butterfly... fly over here...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.720
...ah you've also grown a tail on your butt...

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.720
...drawing on the left, drawing on the right...

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.720
...draw the arrow shaped eye...

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:48.850
...and then another arrow for the other eye...

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.850
...then add two of the wooden horses...

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.940
...stacked right on top of one another...

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.150
...Ku Ku Ku shapes...

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.150
...plus 6 round eyes...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.240
...and there it is, Sana-chan's done!

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.240
Jump, jump... Hey! Hey! hey!

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:05.450
And this is my picture!

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:16.500
Um... I don't have a bone fracture, do I?

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:22.420
Hey? Hello? Excuse me?
Doctor hey hey?

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:26.220
N-No way... I can't dance again?!

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.430
Hmm... well...

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:32.180
You'll be fine in no time! In fact, you can climb Mt. Everest tomorrow!

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.310
Really?

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.650
Yay! "Mou man tai" is Cantonese... "No problem" is English!

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.570
Just say "No problem"!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:47.160
Ah, Kurata is as mischievous as she looks.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.870
Oh, man...

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.410
Yo!

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.120
Ah! You're the guy with no manners from yesterday!

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.370
I have a name you know... Brad.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.040
Why? What are you doing here, huh?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:02.840
Because I wanted to see Kurata.
The feeling was so strong I just flew right over.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.430
Actually, I'm spouting nonsense! My high school is just nearby.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.850
High school?

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.640
He's been cutting school for a few months straight now.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.140
Brad? What are you here for?

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:17.350
Doctor! Don't think I'm being a troublemaker!
I'm actually here to be Kurata's bodyguard.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:20.440
Eh?! I didn't know of such an arrangement!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.820
You better be careful... you two have been targeted.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.330
Wait a minute, what did you mean?!

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.410
There's all sorts of people here.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:36.040
If their acting roles were taken or replaced, who knows what they'll do...

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.540
What's that supposed to mean?

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:47.130
New York is not what you guys think it is.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.640
What kind of joke is this?!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.970
If I'm being attacked because of such small puny matters,

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:56.520
then a few dozen lives aren't enough, is it?!

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:02.400
Whatever... Germans or Americans? Eh?

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.820
Kurata Sana, what's your motive...

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.820
Hey, Brad...

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:13.410
We came here because of the musical, not just for ourselves.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.960
We'd also like to see the audience enjoy watching it...

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:22.500
so could you tell them that our goals are different... if you should see them...

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.590
If I should see them?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.300
It's so painful...

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.260
Get on...

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:35.430
Eh? What?
You want to carry me? No need...

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.680
Kurata really knows nothing, huh?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:42.650
In America, you have to accept a guy's good intentions... if you're a lady...

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.030
Fine, if you say so...

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.870
Actually he's not such a bad guy...

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.580
See ya...

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.080
Thank you very much.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.460
Is it over already?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.390
Naozumi-kun...

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.850
Wh-what in the world happened to you?

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:22.440
Sana-chan, sorry about that...
How's your leg?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.270
Don't worry about that now, what happened to you?

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.400
Did they make a fool out of you?

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:30.150
No, I've just been horribly trained by Michelle-san.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.740
Eh? Michelle-san?

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.660
She said to practice the basics of dancing... I had to do 100 laps on the rooftop.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.450
100 laps?!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:41.040
Then it was 100 pushups and then 100 sit-ups.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.920
These aren't the basics of dance training at all!

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:51.430
She said my dancing experience is too little and my stamina isn't enough.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.140
It's kind of strange...

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.640
What's strange?

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.350
Michelle-san...

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:07.440
I wanted to accompany you to the doctor, but she refused...

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.650
There wasn't a need anyway since the injury wasn't so serious.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.410
It's not that...

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:18.040
I'm sure she doesn't like us at all.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:23.290
Hm, I suppose so... maybe she hasn't really understood us I think.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.580
I guess so...

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:25.330
Of course!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:31.050
Using tedious training for us to keep up, adding tears and sweat on our unfaltering spirits...

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.090
I guess so...

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.510
I guess so...

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:41.060
Definitely, Naozumi-kun!
Hey Naozumi-kun...

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.520
Work hard.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.110
Work hard, ok? The two of us.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:55.530
Sorry. I should be saying that to you.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:58.080
No problem no problem (in Cantonese).

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.290
If it's two people, then we could work hard together, right?

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:03.460
Yeah, if it's two people.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.860
Weird happenings?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.820
Not really, why?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.110
It seems that someone entered here before...

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.570
Even my diary has been
flipped through already.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:40.830
Has anything been stolen?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.910
No, nothing's been stolen.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:48.630
Hmm, who could it have been? Ramsy-san? Michelle-san?

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:51.130
Is there anyone else who's here?

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:55.670
There is the butler Mark, the bodyguard and the chauffeur

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:58.800
and there are other guests
who come in and out.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:02.850
The actual person is Mar...
I can't pronounce it...

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:07.520
You had better be careful...
You two have been targeted.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:11.400
Well, it seems that we've really been targeted, huh?

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:17.110
That can't be, right?
What am I talking about?

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.120
Yo!

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.040
Oh Brad, thanks for just now.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:37.260
It was nothing, your flat chest leaning on my back made me feel really fortunate.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.760
What are you talking about?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:42.680
Oh, angry now, Kurata? Actually you look quite cute like this you know.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:47.230
Geez, you know, you're a real weirdo... what are you doing here?

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:51.100
I'm here to help out. Michelle asked me to dry-clean her clothes.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:55.730
She gets very paranoid when it comes to her clothes... can't be helped.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:57.860
Wow, it's really glamorous.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:00.450
If the tiniest dirt gets on it, she gets mad.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:04.490
If it has anything to do with work, Michelle can get very hysterical.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:08.960
Will she be angry? I thought she was one of those expressionless people.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.960
She's very scary when she's angry.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.420
Anyway, her pride is really high...

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:18.470
...and due to a problem with her role, this thing is turning ugly with Mr. Hamilton...

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:21.840
Probably because he cast the both of you...

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.350
Really...

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.810
They're really disliked by Michelle!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.520
New York.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.570
It's happening again...

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:41.700
I keep having the feeling that we're being spied upon...

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:42.910
OK!

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.410
Hey! Wait a minute!

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:50.500
Hey! You! Wait a minute!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.710
She must be that ghost that Sana-chan mentioned...

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:25.320
Naozumi... so handsome...

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:31.790
A weird beautiful girl appears...

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:31.500
Cute-chan!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:34.420
Eh? A girl?

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.380
It could have been a coincidence...

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:41.340
...but maybe she's the ghost Sana-chan saw last night.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:43.010
Ah, that could be so...

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:46.340
She's been walking up and down in front of Naozumi-kun's room.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:49.510
But she had legs so she couldn't be a ghost anyway.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.680
- Maybe she's a girl who lives here.
- True.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:57.520
But if that's so, then why wasn't she introduced to us? It's really weird.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:07.160
Sorry to keep you waiting,
you may start now.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.100
Thanks for the food.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.610
Please do so.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:50.240
To think... even having meals is so nerve-wracking. It's so tiring.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.540
Yeah, let's turn in early tonight then.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.960
Sana-chan, be careful and remember to lock your door, ok?

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.410
Naozumi-kun, you too.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:57.670
Thanks.

